      "confidence": "high",
      "status": "adjudicated",
      "note": "The authored key stands.  The rule that draws the dots is 3 x n + 2, so figure 20 holds 3 x 20 + 2 = 62.  The blind read chose 59, which is that same rule evaluated at figure 19:  a plain off-by-one, and the option exists to catch it (\"This lands on figure 19\").  The blind pass was given both the caption naming figures 1, 2 and 3 and the rule itself, so nothing was ambiguous.  Recorded because this same item AGREED on the previous run of the identical content;  the disagreement is sampling noise in the blind model, which is the reason disagreements are adjudicated rather than applied.",
