    {
      "itemId": "l3-total-pets",
      "itemHash": "ceb3d7b306af8d01",
      "blind": 1,
      "authored": 2,
      "confidence": "high",
      "status": "adjudicated",
      "note": "The authored key stands, and it is arithmetic rather than interpretation:  the four bars stand at 12, 9, 5, 3, and 12 + 9 + 5 + 3 = 29.  The blind read chose 26, which is the same sum with the shortest bar left out (12 + 9 + 5 = 26).  That is exactly what this distractor exists to catch, its rationale says so, and the passage warns about it in as many words:  \"The TOTAL is every bar added together, including the short ones that are easy to skip.\"  The figure data handed to the blind pass listed all four values, so nothing about the item was ambiguous;  the short bar was dropped, which is the misconception the item is built around and not a second defensible reading.",
      "adjudicatedBy": "Justin Solomon (via Claude Code, 26-0822 WP2 L3)",
      "adjudicatedAt": "2026-08-22"
